# A shop's database remembers each of its migrations by a checksum of the file's exact bytes, and
# refuses to open if the program that reads it was built from other bytes. The line ending is part
# of those bytes, so it must not depend on how a machine has set git up. It is CRLF because that is
# what every database made so far holds. Never change it.
crates/motodesk-server/migrations/*.sql text eol=crlf
